  "reference_answer_text": "③",
  "reference_solution": "[정답] ③\n\n[해설]\n$\\lim_{h \\rightarrow 0} \\frac{f \\left( 1 + 2 h \\right) - 4}{h}$$= 6$이고 $\\lim_{h \\rightarrow 0} h = 0$이므로\n$\\lim_{h \\rightarrow 0} \\left\\{ f \\left( 1 + 2 h \\right) - 4 \\right\\} = 0$, $f \\left( 1 \\right) = 4$\n$\\lim_{h \\rightarrow 0} \\frac{f \\left( 1 + 2 h \\right) - 4}{h}$$= \\lim_{h \\rightarrow 0} \\frac{f \\left( 1 + 2 h \\right) - f \\left( 1 \\right)}{2 h} \\times 2$\n$= f' \\left( 1 \\right) \\times 2 = 6$\n이므로 $f' \\left( 1 \\right) = 3$\n따라서 $f (1) + f' (1) = 4 + 3 = 7$\n",
  "problem_text": "다항함수 $f (x)$에 대하여 $\\lim_{h \\rightarrow 0} \\frac{f \\left( 1 + 2 h \\right) - 4}{h} = 6$일 때, $f (1) + f' (1)$의 값은?\n① $\\mathrm{5}$\t\t② $\\mathrm{6}$\t\t③ $\\mathrm{7}$\n④ $\\mathrm{8}$\t\t⑤ $\\mathrm{9}$\n",
